  "text": "Carrie Hume, VMD, DACVIM (Oncology), WestVet Boise\nFor Pet Parents\nFor Veterinarians\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFind a Clinic\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nFind a Clinic\nReferral Partner Login\nRefer a Patient\nLocations\nFind A Doctor\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nReferral Partner Resources\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFor Pet Parents\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFor Veterinarians\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nRefer a Patient\nFind a Doctor\nCarrie Hume\nCarrie Hume, VMD, DACVIM (Oncology)\nBoard-Certified Veterinary Oncologist\nCarrie Hume, VMD, Diplomate, ACVIM (Oncology), is a Board-certified\nVeterinary Oncologist\nat\nWestVet Boise\n. As a Diplomate, Dr. Hume has received extensive training in veterinary internal medicine, including specific training in the diagnosis and treatment of canine and feline cancer. Her clinical interests include canine and feline lymphoma, canine mast cell tumors, and canine transitional cell carcinoma.\nDr. Carrie Hume, a native of Pennsylvania, completed her undergraduate work at Pennsylvania State University. She earned her Veterinariae Medicinae Doctoris (VMD) degree from the University of Pennsylvania School of Veterinary Medicine in 2003.\nShe then completed a one-year internship in small animal medicine and surgery, at the Matthew J. Ryan Veterinary Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, followed by a three-year small animal oncology residency at the Matthew J. Ryan Veterinary Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania.\nHer husband, Daniel Hume, is also a veterinary specialist at WestVet. They joined the WestVet specialist team in 2013.\nAs the parents of two active daughters and a young son, they enjoy exploring the West and all the outdoor adventures that the Treasure Valley has to offer. In her free time, Dr. Hume enjoys running and hiking.\nEducation & Training\nBachelor's:\nPennsylvania State University\nVeterinary Medicine Doctor:\nUniversity of Pennsylvania School of Veterinary Medicine\nInternship (Rotating Small Animal Medicine and Surgery):\nMatthew J. Ryan Veterinary Hospital\nResidency (Medical Oncology):\nMatthew J. Ryan Veterinary Hospital\nSpecializations\nBoard Certification:\nDiplomate of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine\nSpecialties\nMedical Oncology\nServicing Locations\nWestVet Boise\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to know our specialists better and to show you why we love our team members so much! Meet Dr. Carrie Hume, Veterinary Oncologist at WestVet Boise.\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to know our specialists better and to show you why we love our team members so much! Meet Dr. Carrie Hume, Veterinary Oncologist at WestVet Boise.\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
